{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by means of its scale, bulk, siting, and design, would disrupt the uniform building line and built form of a prominent terrace row within a Neighbourhood Centre and would appear as a discordant addition which fails to appear subordinate to the original building.&nbsp;As a result, it fails to respect or reflect the character and appearance of the original building, terrace row and wider area, causing undue harm to each of these as well as to the street scene along Tanner Street. The proposal therefore fails to accord with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals are of a high quality design which pays regard to the local character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024);Policies D4 &amp; D8 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SP2, DMD1 &amp; DMD3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting and scale, would be an undesirable addition that would cause a significant obstruction along a busy footway of a Neighbourhood Centre.&nbsp;As a result, it would impede pedestrian movement, to the detriment of sustainable and active travel. The proposal thus fails to accord with the following policies which seek to promote the retention and creation of streets which support pedestrian movement and active modes of travel:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024);Policies D3, D8, SD8 and T2 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD1 of&nbsp;The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
